  <layout>One column of italic Latin verse, centred; below it at right a catchword "Latio-". No running head, no page number, no margin notes.</layout>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">Fluentis instar medius aureo templum</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">Sophiaeque doctos imbuit lares fluxu</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">Iam ripa inaudax semiliberumque intra</l>
    <l n="4" para="true">Spatiatus alveum, nec fragosus incedens</l>
    <l n="5" para="true">Nimiusve rerum, iam per aggerem praeceps</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">In obvias se plebis inferens aures</l>
    <l n="7" para="true">Torrentiorem, &amp; incitos simul fastus,</l>
    <l n="8" para="true">Apicesque honoris &amp; superbia colles</l>
    <l n="9" para="true">Altasque scelerum criminumque radices</l>
    <l n="10" para="true">Fundo revellens; saxaque ipsa facunda</l>
    <l n="11" para="true">Convulsa strage tabito emovens limo,</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">Placide verendus: plurimum tamen lene</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">Admurmurantis more rivuli labens,</l>
    <l n="14" para="true">Propter sonori marginem cavum tophi,</l>
    <l n="15" para="true">Quem creber ambiat sititor, illimem</l>
    <l n="16" para="true">Vado videri, &amp; roscidum &amp; suum semper,</l>
    <l n="17" para="true">Animisque titillante cereis flecti,</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">Et gratioso blandus incidens sensu,</l>
    <l n="19" para="true">Prae quam fluentis pura guttula electri,</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">Tenerrimoque vulnerans sono pectu-</l>
    <l n="21">s,</l>
    <l n="22" para="true">Jecurque circum ludibundus &amp; fibris</l>
    <l n="23" para="true">Penitus inerrans. Palpitare tunc castis</l>
    <l n="24" para="true">Corda entheata gaudiis; decentesque</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Ridere fletus, prae dolore, sed lato</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">Singultientes, flere risus, at motu</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">Voluptuoso, quando melleus fandi</l>
    <l n="28" para="true">Danaëio se pondere in sinus ipsos</l>
    <l n="29" para="true">Penetrat imber, atque amabilem plenis</l>
    <l n="30" para="true">Si qua est animula miselia, vagula, sol</l>
    <l n="31" para="true">Rorem propinat poculis. Simul dulcis</l>
    <l n="32" para="true">Siticulosa flore musteo Suadae</l>
    <l n="33" para="true">Inebriatur auris, &amp; simul sancto</l>
    <l n="34" para="true">Lymphatur aestu, seculique despectum</l>
    <l n="35" para="true">Mens &amp; suave tedium imbibit vitae,</l>
    <l n="36" para="true">Ardetque superas jugiter perennantes</l>
    <l n="37" para="true">Non eloquendi fluminis cataractas,</l>
    <l n="38" para="true">De fonte caelum purius refundentes,</l>
    <l n="39" para="true">Lautamque vivis amphoris sitim stinguit</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">Sub vorticosi mersa Numinis lymphis.</l>
    <l n="41" para="true">Verende WITSI, cujus insidens labris</l>
    <l n="42" para="true">Divina Peitho sacro sancta stillantem</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">Latio-</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The last line "Latio-" stands at the lower right as a catchword. Some words are doubtful in the scan (e.g. "Peitho", "tophi", "electri", "miselia"); the faint marks at the page edges are specks, not text.</notes>
